@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L66), [acceptance](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property with its path and expected type without leaking the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L111), [validated by: logs the failing property path without the rejected value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L175), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults.
+- When an input violates an `enum`, the rejection names the failing property path and the `enum` constraint without including the rejected value ([validated by: names the enum constraint when rejecting an unlisted value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L141)).
+- An input that satisfies its schema keeps undeclared properties when it reaches the executor ([validated by: passes valid input and unlisted properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L47)).
+- Validation log records name the failing property path and constraint, including the missing property for a `required` failure ([validated by: logs the missing required property path and constraint](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L92)).
+- A missing required property nested inside an object is reported with its complete field path, including the parent path ([validated by: reports the complete path for a nested missing required property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L255)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L249)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L162)).
+- An invalid static schema is rejected synchronously at registration, and the error names the tool being registered ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L196)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L211)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- A tool call causes another provider round, and streamed chunks from both rounds remain in order ([validated by: runs another round after a tool call and streams both rounds in order](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L455)).
+- A response that requests no tool stops after one provider round ([validated by: stops after one round when nothing asked for a tool](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L467)).
+- A tool result rewrites an upserted entry's index to the session index ([validated by: appends an upserted entry to the session and rewrites its index to match](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L503)).
+- A tool result that marks the assistant response handled emits suppression ([validated by: asks for suppression when the tool says the reply is already handled](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L520)).
+- Text from each provider round is joined before the post-response hook runs ([validated by: joins the text of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L532)).
+- Usage reported by an earlier provider round is retained when a later round reports none ([validated by: keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L554)).
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so it can retry with corrected input](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L401), [acceptance](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
